s/IridiumMaster/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"A long first line in an unbracketed keystroke paste was being sent immediately by rule #22. Hold that ambiguous Enter for 32 ms: following text or Enter makes it a newline, while silence submits the single-line prompt once. The named window spans four existing 8 ms burst intervals; controlled-clock tests cover continuation through 31 ms and submission at 32 ms.\n\nBracketed paste, Tab, and modified submit bindings keep their existing behavior. Delayed results use the normal submission path in chat, embedded forms, and cloud tasks. Cancellation, overlays, and draft replacement disarm the pending submission.\n\nOwner decision D642(c); refs #2312. Bounded fix under **Product principles**: “Maintain continuous Codex parity without removing Corbanu-specific behavior.”\n\nValidation:\n- Regression fails on main by submitting the first pasted line; passes with this fix. Existing #22 submission assertions remain, with checks for the authorized delay.\n- Rust 1.99.1: clippy with warnings denied for codex-tui and codex-cloud-tasks; 4,811 library tests passed, six existing skips.\n- Seven real PTY scenarios passed against loopback inference with synthetic credentials: fast single-line input, multiline raw-key paste including blank lines and Unicode, bracketed paste, Escape/Ctrl+C cancellation and recovery. Exactly five requests with exact prompt contents.\n- One new multiline composer snapshot reviewed individually; release-note validation and formatting pass.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-16T10:57:09Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T12:38:33Z","closed_at":"2026-11-16T12:38:33Z","merged_at":"2026-11-16T12:38:33Z","merge_commit_sha":"f5e7670323579ed359c8040c908d9139612b900d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"CorbanuCore:astra-d642","ref":"astra-d642","repo":{"id":1283517261,"n